From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juan Pablo Lassala <jpablolassala@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 09:11:12 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] applet: Add a Caminito backend

Caminito, the Wayland compositor for MATE, knows which window has the
focus and where that window's menu is on the bus, as a Wayland panel
cannot: the menu is tied to a surface. It publishes the focused window's
menu as the GlobalMenu property of org.mate.Caminito, with the kind of
menu, the bus name that serves it, its object paths and the application's
id.

When org.mate.Caminito has an owner, draw that menu in place of the one
the window manager backend finds, and ask for no registrar: Caminito
tells the apps itself when to give up their menubars. It does so while
org.mate.Caminito.GlobalMenuApplet has an owner, so own that name from the
first applet added until the last one is destroyed.

mate-panel loads on Wayland only the applets that say they run there, so
say so. Without an owner of org.mate.Caminito, nothing else changes.
---
 data/appmenu-mate.plugin.desktop.in |   1 +
 lib/appmenu-abstractions.vala       |   7 +-
 lib/appmenu-caminito.vala           | 207 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 lib/menu-widget.vala                |  26 +++-
 lib/meson.build                     |   1 +
 5 files changed, 240 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 lib/appmenu-caminito.vala

